-- title:
--   Tagged cube points
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that a real Banach space $X$ with the approximation property is K-convex (the Rademacher projection is bounded on $L_2(\{\pm1\}^n;X)$ uniformly in $n$) if and only if $X$ and its dual $X^*$ both have finite cotype. The converse direction shows that such $X$ has nontrivial type, i.e. does not contain $\ell_1^n$ uniformly, and then derives K-convexity from a power-gap estimate for commuting coordinate projections. Work in $\{0,1\}^{k+m+m}$.
--
--   1. **Tagged primal points.** $u_i$ followed by the unit vector $e_i$ and zeros:
--   $$
--   \tilde U_i=(u_i,\ e_i,\ 0) .
--   $$
--   2. **Tagged dual points.** $\tilde V_j=(v_j,\ (D_{ij})_i,\ e_j)$ for a sign matrix $D$, so that $w_{\tilde V_j}(\tilde U_i)=w_{v_j}(u_i)(-1)^{D_{ij}}$.
--   3. **Tagged covectors.** $(v,s,e_0)$ for a vector $v$ and a column pattern $s$. The tags make the frames linearly independent and encode prescribed sign patterns.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Cotype/TaggedFrames.lean

